{/eq}
This means that the sum we are looking for, is {eq}f(4) + f(5) + f(6)

{/eq}
Now, for this problem, {eq}f(4) = \binom{11}{4-2} =?=220{/eq}
{eq}f(5) = \binom{11}{5-2} =?=165{/eq}
{eq}f(6) = \binom{11}{6-2} =?=84{/eq}

Adding them together, we get the answer:


