draw(A--P^^B--Q);
label("$A$",A,N); label("$B$",B,W); label("$C$",C,E); label("$P$",P,S); label("$Q$",Q,E); label("$H$",H,NW);
draw(rightanglemark(A,P,B,3.5));
draw(rightanglemark(A,Q,B,3.5));
draw(rightanglemark(A,L,C,3.5));
label("$3$",usecircle(L--A,1/3),NE); label("$2$",usecircle(A--H,1/3),NW);
label("$2$",usecircle(H--B,1/3),SE); label("$5$",usecircle(C--L,1/3),S); label("$5$",midpoint(C--H),S);[/asy]
In conclusion, even though there was no problem in the whole computation path,Attention to detail played a very large role in efficiently identifying $HP/HQ=3/1$, hence it becomes easier to know that the answer is simply $3^2-1^2$ cubes in number.
